  "core_review": [
    "K1 and K4 full rollouts have equal nominal gameplay frames and 128 nominal Adam steps. The frame-target collector retains the full crossing vector call, slices unused rows, values the final next state before resets, and skips reset after budget closure.",
    "GAE masks bootstrap on termination, bootstraps truncations and live rollout tails, and stops recurrence at termination or truncation.",
    "K1 gamma and lambda fourth roots match K4 decay across four-frame decision boundaries. K4 aggregates within-call score and alive rewards without internal discounting, so the match does not reproduce exact per-frame reward weighting inside a K4 call.",
    "Advantages normalize over the full macrobatch. Weighted 512-sample microbatches accumulate gradients into one 2048-sample optimizer step, followed by one global clip and Adam step. KL uses the full rollout at epoch end.",
    "Explicit per-slot seed streams bind native episode indices and actual seeds. Sampling is with replacement, so repeated actual seed values across slots are valid; uniqueness applies to slot identities, not seed values.",
    "Recovery snapshots follow successful PPO transaction boundaries and store learner, optimizer, RNG, counters, native episode metadata, and hashes. They do not capture full simulator state, are not evaluated or selected, and grant no automatic resume."
  ],
